<span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
<h2>What buyers still want to know</h2>
</div>
<div>
<div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Are expensive wireless earbuds worth it?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Only if you need a specific premium advantage, like stronger ANC, better call quality, or tight iPhone integration. For most people, the better decision is a mature midrange model with lower regret if the battery ages or the fit is imperfect.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Should I buy wireless earbuds based on sound quality?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Sound matters, but it should not be the only filter. Fit, battery consistency, connection stability, app behavior, and warranty support usually matter more in daily ownership.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Why not just buy AirPods?</summary><p class="faq-answer">AirPods make the most sense for iPhone-first buyers. They are not the best universal decision because many of their strongest benefits depend on Apple devices, and repairability remains poor.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>How long should wireless earbuds last?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Most people should think of wireless earbuds as a limited-life product. The batteries are tiny, sealed, and difficult to replace. That is why paying less for a reliable midrange model often makes more sense than stretching for a flagship.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>What matters more: ANC or fit?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Fit comes first. Poor fit weakens sound, comfort, call quality, and noise cancellation. Strong ANC cannot fully fix earbuds that do not seal or stay in place.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Should I avoid renewed or refurbished earbuds?</summary><p class="faq-answer">For this category, usually yes. Earbuds are worn in-ear, battery health is hard to judge, and small accessories like tips and cases matter. A clean new listing is safer.</p></details>
</div>
</div>
